       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is about five times the maximum labeled dose of 200 mg. I know of no indication that supports it, and it could seriously harm a 70 kg patient with normal organ function. You haven't given a clinical rationale, and a note on the order wouldn't make it safer.\n\nHere's what I can do:\n- Enter sertraline at a dose within the labeled range, such as 50, 100, or 200 mg by mouth once daily.\n- Enter a different order if the intent was something else, such as another drug or a taper or titration plan.\n\nIf you believe this dose is warranted, for example in a protocol or special circumstance I don't know about, I'd suggest discussing it with pharmacy or toxicology. They can review it and enter it through the appropriate channel with the right safeguards.\n\nIf the patient may have taken an overdose, that needs poison control or toxicology involved right away. I can't treat an overdose by entering a daily order.\n\nWhich dose would you like me to enter?"
